    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0194" n="172" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg172"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/11–1951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d113-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-19T00:00:00+01:00">November 19,
                            1951—midnight.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Delga 260. For Hickerson<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d113-f2"/> (UNA) and Ingram (UNI) from Hall.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d113-f3"/> Re
                    contributions. Essential contributions position be presented delegation week Nov
                    19. In absence Congressional consultations and <pb facs="0195" n="173"
                        xml:id="pg173"/> based upon discussions Congressmen Vorys and
                        Mansfield<anchor n="4" xml:id="d113-f4"/>
                    USGADel advisers believe positions stated in
                        SD/A/C.5/170 must be modified as fols:</p>
                <p>US shld propose contributions comite report be referred to a subcomite with
                    instructions so to revise report as to reduce US contribution to 33⅓ percent and
                    to increase contributions of countries presently under-assessed sufficiently to
                    offset decrease in US contribution.</p>
                <p>If this position is not accepted US shld vote against comite report to comply
                    with appropriation statute and state that del
                    has no authority to commit in any way US Govt to payment of any contribution in
                    excess of one third of total cost of UN during
                    fiscal year 1952.</p>
                <p>This position is subj to approval of USGADel
                    but represents maximum which Congressmen Vorys and Mansfield feel can be
                    presented to Congress in absence of Congressional consultation required by
                    Appropriation Act. Need reply by 9 a.m. Wed Paris time.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d113-f5"/> [Hall.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d113-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d113-f1-content">
                <p>The Secretary of State was in Paris at this time serving as Chairman of the U.S.
                    Delegation to the General Assembly. The session convened in Paris on November
                    6.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d113-f2" n="2" xml:id="d113-f2-content">
                <p>John D. Hickerson, Assistant Secretary of State for United Nations Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d113-f3" n="3" xml:id="d113-f3-content">
                <p>William O. Hall, Director of the Office of International Administration and
                    Conferences and member of the Advisory Staff of the U.S. Delegation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d113-f4" n="4" xml:id="d113-f4-content">
                <p>John M. Vorys and Michael J. Mansfield, of the House of Representatives, members
                    of the U.S. Delegation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d113-f5" n="5" xml:id="d113-f5-content">
                <p>Notation at the end of the telegram: “No legal obstacle to voting for report.
                    Disastrous to vote against it. Least should be abstain. Recognize essentially
                    prolem of Congress[ional] relat[ion]s.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
